It's not an erratum. It falls outside the scope of what the book
promises to deliver. (The book does deliver what it promises.)

Lojbans Central and Peripheral have said loud and clear many times
that the semantics is incomplete (both in the sense that stuff that
has been decided hasn't been properly documented, and in the sense
that a lot of stuff hasn't even been decided). The way for it to be
completed is both through usage and through jboske (by which I mean
not that group of a**holes on that other list, bur rather the 
process of deducing what has not been decided from what has been 
decided). Lojban is not a finished product. You are part of the
process of bringing it into being.

